            'excerpt' => 'Find out which xTool laser accessories are worth buying first for safety, which to add later for tumblers, batches and new materials, and which to skip.',
            'blocks'  => [
                [ 'p', 'The xTool laser accessories worth buying first are the ones that protect people and the room: an air purifier or a fan that vents fumes outside, plus an automatic fire safety set on machines that support it. Add a rotary, a conveyor or an extra laser module only for specific jobs. Before every purchase, check compatibility – many xTool accessories fit only selected machines.' ],
                [ 'p', 'Below we map xTool accessories to the machines in our demo set – P3, M2, F2, F2 Ultra, F2 Ultra UV and MetalFab – as well as the S1 and X1.' ],
                [ 'h2', 'What should you buy first for a laser engraver?' ],
                [ 'p', 'Cutting and engraving produce smoke and dust, and the material can catch fire, so the first money goes on fume extraction and fire protection. We cover laser classes and safe working in a separate article.' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Fume extraction: inline fan or air purifier' ],
                [ 'p', 'Match extraction to the machine, materials and workspace. The SafetyPro IF2 2.0 inline fan can exhaust fumes outdoors; xTool specifies two 14,000 rpm fans. A purifier recirculates air, but no filter removes every gas. Check the manufacturer’s requirements and installation conditions; lack of odour does not prove that air is safe:' ],
