                [ 'p', 'The Fire Safety Set works with compatible machines to activate fire suppression and also has a manual trigger. Install and inspect it according to the instructions, including checking the extinguishing agent. Never leave a running laser unattended. According to xTool, using the first-generation Fire Safety Set with the M2 and an xTool Inline Duct Fan or xTool Smoke Purifier requires a separately purchased smart switch for successful fire suppression. Set 2 fits the X1 and M2; the first version fits the S1, F2 Ultra, F2 Ultra UV, F1 Ultra and M2. The F2 and P3 are not on the stated compatibility list.' ],
                [ 'products', '8762129842389,8032675234005,7954661376213' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Safety goggles – not for every machine' ],
                [ 'p', 'The M2, S1 and X1 are described as enclosed Class 1 machines; use them with the enclosure closed as instructed. Do not bypass interlocks or run a laser with the enclosure open merely because you have goggles. If the manual permits work with access to the beam, a controlled area and eye protection selected for the laser parameters are required. xTool lists goggles for 316–460 nm, 630–670 nm and 800–1080 nm, but not CO₂ (10,600 nm). Protection ratings vary by band; select OD and LB markings for the model, wavelengths and operating conditions according to the manual.' ],
                [ 'h2', 'Rotary attachment: RA3 or RA2 Pro?' ],
                [ 'p', 'Tumblers, bottles and rings are engraved with a rotary attachment. Buy one when you have such orders, and check compatibility:' ],
